{"chunk_id": "b02f32cc9d1f", "text": "This section recounts the mythic conflict surrounding Daksha\u2019s sacrifice and Shiva\u2019s exclusion from the sacrificial order. When Uma (Parvati) laments that the gods deny Mahadeva a share of sacrificial offerings, Shiva unleashes his wrath. He storms Daksha\u2019s ritual with terrifying followers, destroying the sacrifice; from a drop of his sweat arises a dreadful being that consumes the personified Sacrifice and terrifies gods and sages. Brahma intervenes, granting Shiva a rightful share in all sacrifices and asking that the destructive force be restrained. The being born of Shiva\u2019s sweat becomes \u201cFever,\u201d whose power is dispersed across diseases and disturbances in animals, nature, and humans. The narrative frames cosmic disorder as the result of disrespecting Shiva and explains illness as a manifestation of his dispersed energy.\nShiva destroys Daksha\u2019s sacrifice after being excluded, creates the being Fever from his wrath, and ultimately gains a share of sacrificial offerings.\nThemes: divine wrath, sacrificial ritual conflict, origin of disease, Shiva\u2019s supremacy, cosmic disorder and restoration", "vector": [0.002664459403604269, -0.005796545185148716, -0.004676260985434055, -0.013524150475859642, -0.03369599208235741, 0.021369503811001778, -0.03261944279074669, -0.025056684389710426, -0.009655301459133625, -0.013355939649045467, 0.008323071524500847, 0.0166326854377985, 0.016377005726099014, 0.004938669968396425, -0.00017977532115764916, 0.0068024457432329655, 0.04804101213812828, -0.004952126648277044, 0.0246664360165596, 0.004723359830677509, 0.007414733059704304, 0.00782516784965992, 0.012662910856306553, 0.026402371004223824, -0.015623421408236027, 0.0075022028759121895, 0.01057036779820919, -0.021181106567382812, 0.005476944614201784, 0.00525154173374176, 0.0014794141752645373, -0.02493557333946228, -0.0033743090461939573, -0.007394548039883375, -0.034503404051065445, -0.00188396126031